        <p>FISHING.</p>
        <p>I'm very fond of fishing : It is the bost of fun To sit upon the river hank And fish till day is done.</p>
        <p>Sometimes I catch a lot of fish; That's very good for me, Sometimes I only catch a cold Then mother's cross with me.</p>
        <p>Sometimes I never get a bite, \.„, Not with the best of bait ; But still I know the fish will come, . If I can only wait.</p>
        <p>Last Monday was a holiday, I caught two nice fat fish, I thought I'd take them home for tea, They'd make a lovely dish.</p>
        <p>'Silt while I was n-fishing, Our naughty terrier Jack Caine quietly and stole the best Behind my very back,</p>
