 was decided to take no action in the matter. THE BOLTON SCHOOL PLANS. limelight). The proceeds will be devoted to the choir fund. The Mayor has been re-appointed chairman of the Sites and Buildings Committee. A letter was read at a meeting on April 6th intimating that, at a special meeting of the Town Council held on 'i the 19th March, 1906, the confirmation of the Council Ito two resolutions of the Education Committee at their</p>
        <p>......... meetmgs on the 20th March. 1905, and the 19th February, 1906, respectively, which was given on the 11th April, 1903, and the 6th March, 1906, was rescinded. A letter was also read, dated the 29th March, 1906, from the Board of Education, enquiring "what progress is being made with the building of the new Latchford Council school which is to replace the temporary school</p>
        <p>in Grappenhall-road." The matter was adjourned until April 9. On that date the committee met again, and proceeded to the adjourned consideration of the plans, Ste., of the "Bolton "Council school, and, in accordance with the committee's request, the Architects for the erection of 'hat school attended the meeting and submitted their ;Views to the committee. After a lengthy discussion, it was decided to defer consideration of the matter to a later meeting, in order that the architects may submit, in writing, their views for the consideration of the committee.</p>
