      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-21_WidnesExaminer_art0177" n="art0177">
        <head>WARRINGTON CO-OPERATIVE SOCIETY.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON CO-OPERATIVE SOCIETY.</p>
        <p>Quarterly Meeting.</p>
        <p>The quarterly meeting of the Warrington Equitable Industrial Co-operative Society, Limitedowas held in the Co-operative Hall, Sankey-street, on Wednesday evening. Mr. Thomas Critchley (president) presided over a fair attendance.</p>
        <p>THE BALANCE SHEET. The committee reported that the sales for the quarter amounted to £33,318 175., which was .£543 14s. 4d. les,s than the previous quarter, but compared with the corresponding quarter of last year showed an increase of £1,737 Gs. 10d. The committee obtained possession from the builders of the new branch in L-atchford on Tuesday, April 10th, and hoped to have everything arranged for opening on Wednesday, April 17th. They trusted members would give it that support which would enable them to make it as successful as any of the other branches. Some difficulty might arise with respect to the delivery of goods, as Latchford covered a large district. They hoped that while they had gone to this great expense in meeting the require- ments of the district that members would not be too exacting in their demands in out-of-the-way places. The PRESIDENT said the committee had pleasure in presenting such a very satisfactory balance sheet as the large advance in the amount of transactions showed that co-operation was still on the increase in Warring- ton as well as in other parts of the country. He read an extract from a co-operative journal in which it was pointed out that a syndicate was being formed by manu- facturers of certain special articles and that it declined to supply co-operative societies with goods if the societies gave a dividend on them. The result was that I the Co-operative Societies had to decide whether to sell the goods at all or whether to sell them without a I dividend. The Warrington Society had decided not to , sell them, but the Wholesale Co-operative Society would supply articles as like them as possible. Mr. ; Critchley referred to the opening this week of the , Latchford branch, and said he trusted it would be a successful undertaking. They had two splendid shops and a warehouse, and he looked forward to a large increase in sales and membership as a consequence of the opening of the branch. During the discussion which followed a member asked if the balance sheet could not be issued earlier than the night of the quarterly meeting. It was utterly impos- sible in the few minutes at their disposal to go through the items properly. After considerable discussion the PRESIDENt promised that the Committee would do their best to have the balance sheet placed in thhops on the Satur- day morning previous to the quarterlymeeting. The balance sheet was adopted. THE PAST YEAR'S RECORD. Mr. RATITBONE reported that the , sales for 1905 amounted to £151,117 10s. 4d., as against £144,633, the previous year. During the quarter just concluded 1,207 members had joined and 928 withdrawn</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-21_WidnesExaminer_art0178" n="art0178">
        <head>SUGGESTION'S.</head>
        <p>SUGGESTION'S.</p>
        <p>A MEMBER proposed that the Society should iSSIIO an almanack eachlyear, containing information with refer- ence to the movement. Mr. JAMES CROWTHER seconded. Mr. F. FARRAR said the proposal was unnecessary. There were over 8,000 members and the expenditure would be a serious item, and he did not think the outlay would be justified by the results. A general discussion followed as to the best methods of bringing about a larger attendance at quarterly meetings. Mr. W. If mon suggested the holding of lectures. Finally at the suggestion of the CHAIRMAN, the motion that an al manack be presented was withdmwn,the t2hairman promising that the Committee would consider the best means of creating more interest in co-operation.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-21_WidnesExaminer_art0179" n="art0179">
