      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-21_WidnesExaminer_art0183" n="art0183">
        <head>ST. LUKE'S CHURCH.</head>
        <p>ST. LUKE'S CHURCH.</p>
        <p>The vestry meeting was held on Thursday evening the Rev. H. H. Wild (curate-in-charge) presiding.—The accounts which showed a credit balance of Ll 195.10 d. were passed—The, following officers were elected : Wardens, Messrs. Jackson and Oldfield ; sidesmen, Messrs. H. Graham, J. Peers, H. Dean, T. Ellison, J. Warburton, C. Dendy, R. Armstrong, H. Taylor, A. Hewitt, C. H. Massey, T. Taker, and Tort ; auditors, lessrs. Ashcroft and Horrabin.—A vote of thanks was accorded to Mr. Lord for his gift of trees and the plant- ing of the same in the church yard—The officers,choir and Sunday school teachers were cordially thanked for their services—The meeting closed with a vote of thanks to the chairman. Mr. Wild remarked that the past year had been a successful one in every way and he had reason to hope that the coming year would be equally satisfactory.</p>
